REVIEWER: In both `RenderWidgetHostViewAura::AddedToRootWindow()` and `RenderWidgetHostViewAndroid::OnAttachedToWindow()` (`render_widget_host_view_android.cc:3395-3396`), `UpdateScreenInfo()` is called immediately before `host()->SetDeferVisualProperties(false)`. Because `defer_visual_properties_` is still `true` during `UpdateScreenInfo()`, `host()->NotifyScreenInfoChanged()` (`SynchronizeVisualPropertiesIgnoringPendingAck()`) early-returns `false` (after clearing `visual_properties_ack_pending_`), and on Android `OnSynchronizedDisplayPropertiesChanged()` allocates a new `viz::LocalSurfaceId` whose sync is dropped until `SetDeferVisualProperties(false)` calls `SynchronizeVisualProperties()` (`ignore_ack = false`) on the next line.

Consider calling `host()->SetDeferVisualProperties(false)` before `UpdateScreenInfo()` in both places so `UpdateScreenInfo()` can synchronize with its intended `ignore_ack` semantics:
```cpp
  window_->GetHost()->AddObserver(this);
  host()->SetDeferVisualProperties(false);
  UpdateScreenInfo();
```
OWNER: No, we should not flip this order. The call order `UpdateScreenInfo` -> `SetDeferVisualProperties(false)` triggers only one visual sync IPC, whereas the suggested order will trigger twice. Also, the first of the 2 IPCs (triggered by `SetDeferVisualProperties(false)`) may contain stale data, because only `UpdateScreenInfo` updates the scren info.

