REVIEWER: We could just check whether the remote is bound and `document_->IsActive()` is an invariant to assert alongside that.  Not sure if there are any other reasons why the remote would be reset in the future.

```suggestion
if (model_context_host_remote_.is_bound()) {
  CHECK(document_->IsActive());
  model_context_host_remote_->UnregisterScriptTool(tool_id);
}
```
OWNER: There shouldn't be any other reasons. I prefer checking `IsActive()` because it's the higher-level condition we actually care about checking for after script execution. It's also exactly what the spec will condition off of, since it's general best practice that only active documents can reach out to the browser or start work in parallel. So after running script, what we guard against is the document becoming inactive. The remote being reset is just an implementation detail of that.

So if anything, I'd prefer reversing this, and conditioning on `IsActive()` and having the invariant `CHECK(model_context_host_remote_.is_bound())`; however, since I don't see that invariant basically anywhere else in the code base, I think I'd prefer to keep as-is.

