REVIEWER: Skipping here removes both the length prefix and the NAL bytes from the
converted buffer, but leaves `subsamples` describing the original layout.
Its total will therefore exceed the converted buffer size, and the
CENC/CBCS decryptors will reject the sample via
`VerifySubsamplesMatchSize()`.

This does not require rejecting every sample with non-empty subsamples. If
the complete removed range is clear, deleting it is safe because clear bytes
do not consume or reorder the cipher stream. Please subtract
`length_size + nal_length` from the affected `clear_bytes`. If any part of
the range overlaps `cypher_bytes`, do not skip this NAL; preserve the old
conversion behavior instead.

```
const size_t bytes_to_remove = length_size + nal_length;
const size_t output_offset = buffer->size();

if (ShouldSkipDummyNALU(codec, nalu) &&
    IsRangeClear(*subsamples, output_offset, bytes_to_remove)) {
  RemoveClearRange(subsamples, output_offset, bytes_to_remove);
  pos += nal_length;
  continue;
}

// If the range intersects ciphertext, fall through and emit the NAL.
```
